                {
                    "is_best": true,
                    "html": "<div class=\"reply__content post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Don't rely on the CubeMx figure, it's just a photo.</p>\n<p>Please check the <a href=\"https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/dm00037051.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">datasheet</a> / Figure 76. LQFP64 - Outline</p>\n<p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"mALLEm_0-1775855630289.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"mALLEm_0-1775855630289.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/5373af38-77f3-c116-2422-8fc52d2fc60a.png\" title=\"mALLEm_0-1775855630289.png\"/></span></p>\n<p>And this is pin 1:</p>\n<p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"mALLEm_1-1775855673525.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"mALLEm_1-1775855673525.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/4361a883-e4dc-752a-01cd-e13fa1297144.png\" title=\"mALLEm_1-1775855673525.png\"/></span>.</p>\n<p>In CubeMx: VBAT is indeed pin 1. But your reference of the package on the PCB is wrong.</p>\n<p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"mALLEm_0-1775856130578.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"mALLEm_0-1775856130578.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/0608c2fa-68e8-bfae-19f3-5fc3182b6ce2.png\" title=\"mALLEm_0-1775856130578.png\"/></span></p></div>",
                    "author": "mƎALLEm",
                    "role": "ST Technical Moderator"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Schematic looks okay.</p><p>Is VCAP around 1.2 V?</p><p>Is the chip oriented correctly? Show a picture of the board.</p><p> </p></div>",
                    "author": "TDK",
                    "role": ""
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>VCAP at 1.2V? Do you mean the voltage across it? If so, I can't check it anymore since I just removed those caps to use them in a PCB that I need urgently done. As for the orientation, it's oriented correctly; I triple-checked. Here is a picture: <span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"IMG_20260410_193713_edit_486460115641916.jpg\" style=\"width: 874px;\"><img alt=\"IMG_20260410_193713_edit_486460115641916.jpg\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/691642c5-9862-3a09-7b81-70d2559b7d5d.jpg\" title=\"IMG_20260410_193713_edit_486460115641916.jpg\"/></span></p></div>",
                    "author": "rayboum",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>I suspect Pin 1 is at the lower right corner in this picture, not the lower left like it needs to be.</p><p>Which way is the text on the MCU oriented?</p><p> </p></div>",
                    "author": "Chris21",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Oh no, I clicked on \"accepted as solution\" instead of \"reply.\" How do I undo this?</p><p>The PCB is oriented correctly; the text is just flipped 180 degrees since it's intended to be read from that orientation:</p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"IMG_20260410_204734.jpg\" style=\"width: 874px;\"><img alt=\"IMG_20260410_204734.jpg\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/9e83b5c0-d80f-a106-4c0f-3f149aa75827.jpg\" title=\"IMG_20260410_204734.jpg\"/></span><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"IMG_20260410_204814.jpg\" style=\"width: 749px;\"><img alt=\"IMG_20260410_204814.jpg\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/795dc70d-0850-ce8b-29a5-70849f6c75e5.jpg\" title=\"IMG_20260410_204814.jpg\"/></span><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\" style=\"width: 999px;\"><img alt=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/7c495b49-6f91-5870-cd46-17d28eefad0a.jpg\" title=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\"/></span></p></div>",
                    "author": "rayboum",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Look at this <a href=\"https://community.st.com/t5/stm32-mcus-products/stm32f401-64pin-pin1-marking-orientation/td-p/419306\" target=\"_blank\">post</a>.</p></div>",
                    "author": "mƎALLEm",
                    "role": "ST Technical Moderator"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Ok, so from what I understand, this pinout diagram I followed is faulty, as pin 1 (VBAT in the STM32F405 case) is shown at the very top of the row next to the pin 1 indicator and not directly next to it. Is this correct?</p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\" style=\"width: 999px;\"><img alt=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/16dec6dd-5869-eb6a-a4fd-1b2def2bd016.jpg\" title=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\"/></span></p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"rayboum_2-1775855403925.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"rayboum_2-1775855403925.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/eacc812b-7c3e-3065-5ab9-8dae3d60d42e.png\" title=\"rayboum_2-1775855403925.png\"/></span></p><p> </p></div>",
                    "author": "rayboum",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"Chris21_0-1775851207569.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"Chris21_0-1775851207569.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/2ed59e8f-196b-022f-5d19-a10628648933.png\" title=\"Chris21_0-1775851207569.png\"/></span></p><p>If the MCU labeling (text printed on the chip) is not right side up in your photo, pin1 is not at the lower left corner.</p></div>",
                    "author": "Chris21",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>I followed this pinout diagram. Is it wrong?</p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\" style=\"width: 999px;\"><img alt=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/2bbf326d-1153-2bdd-9095-475561c50353.jpg\" title=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\"/></span></p><p>VBAT is pin 1.</p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"rayboum_1-1775854991793.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"rayboum_1-1775854991793.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/a18bac85-e766-4949-c74a-9f08f02d3a3c.png\" title=\"rayboum_1-1775854991793.png\"/></span></p><p> </p></div>",
                    "author": "rayboum",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p><em>&gt; VCAP at 1.2V? Do you mean the voltage across it? If so, I can't check it anymore since I just removed those caps to use them in a PCB that I need urgently done.</em></p><p>Yes.</p><p><em>&gt; As for the orientation, it's oriented correctly; I triple-checked.</em></p><p>How exactly did you check?</p><p>The part is oriented wrong, *and* it is now missing VCAP capacitors. Both of these are showstoppers. You will have to fix both of those. It is possible there are other issues. The soldering does not inspire confidence, but the picture is too blurry to spot any particular issues.</p></div>",
                    "author": "TDK",
                    "role": ""
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Yeah, the VCAP will have to wait until I buy more since I urgently need them, and I only had those 2. But when they were still on this board (4 hours ago), the problem mentioned was still persisting.</p><p>For the orientation, I followed this schematic I found: </p><p>Over here we can see that pin 1 is VBAT:</p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"rayboum_0-1775854115138.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"rayboum_0-1775854115138.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/1085bded-59a7-3280-3343-a8a2415e3848.png\" title=\"rayboum_0-1775854115138.png\"/></span></p><p>Following this schematic, pin 1 is directly above the smaller identifier:</p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\" style=\"width: 999px;\"><img alt=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/630d28fb-93eb-71a4-51ab-81c2f7476f1f.jpg\" title=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\"/></span></p><p>According to my PCB layout, pin 1 is to the bottom right of the stm32F405 lable:</p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"IMG_20260410_204814.jpg\" style=\"width: 749px;\"><img alt=\"IMG_20260410_204814.jpg\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/ea03afc2-e355-7a32-58aa-4c59a6ccd877.jpg\" title=\"IMG_20260410_204814.jpg\"/></span></p><p>And that means it's the bottom left first pin in this picture since it's turned on its right side, and we can see the smaller identifier is under that row of pins, so I think it's oriented correctly unless the first schematic is wrong:</p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"IMG_20260410_204734.jpg\" style=\"width: 874px;\"><img alt=\"IMG_20260410_204734.jpg\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/88d3a8a2-e2b3-ba54-fd29-5f7b9d5ceb82.jpg\" title=\"IMG_20260410_204734.jpg\"/></span></p></div>",
                    "author": "rayboum",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>VBAT is pin 1.  But where is pin 1 on the package?</p><p>Read my previous post.</p></div>",
                    "author": "Chris21",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Yeah, I have read it seems that the pinout diagram i followed was wrong, as pin 1 VBAT is shown to be at the very top of the row that's next to the PIN indicator instead of next to it and i found this other diagram that seems to confirm my suspicions:</p><p>-the faulty one I used:<span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\" style=\"width: 999px;\"><img alt=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/d7a03764-b9b7-853c-d5da-57e7b0849d70.jpg\" title=\"Screenshot_20260410_204438.jpg\"/></span></p><p>- the one from the Utmel website and the STM32CubeMX interface:</p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"rayboum_0-1775855942390.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"rayboum_0-1775855942390.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/8a373182-1eac-241e-fbde-d6004500fa0b.png\" title=\"rayboum_0-1775855942390.png\"/></span></p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"rayboum_1-1775855947741.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"rayboum_1-1775855947741.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/309ca57c-725a-3a6e-7631-8115c57b7f00.png\" title=\"rayboum_1-1775855947741.png\"/></span></p><p> </p></div>",
                    "author": "rayboum",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>See new post from TDK: <a href=\"https://community.st.com/t5/stm32cubemx-mcus/the-chip-text-orientation-in-stm32cubemx-mx2-does-not-match/td-p/891584\" target=\"_blank\">https://community.st.com/t5/stm32cubemx-mcus/the-chip-text-orientation-in-stm32cubemx-mx2-does-not-match/td-p/891584</a></p><p> </p></div>",
                    "author": "Chris21",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                },
                {
                    "is_best": false,
                    "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Personally, I don't think that datasheet is very clear.  TN1433 (Reference device marking schematics for STM32 microcontrollers) is better:</p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"Chris21_0-1775855907987.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"Chris21_0-1775855907987.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/c4fbfb7a-dafa-808b-c049-6bb792771174.png\" title=\"Chris21_0-1775855907987.png\"/></span></p><p>Especially as the datasheet also has this:  </p><p><span class=\"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-inline\" image-alt=\"Chris21_0-1775856334974.png\" style=\"width: 400px;\"><img alt=\"Chris21_0-1775856334974.png\" role=\"button\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/c52a31a2-f7b6-d72f-52f0-e8db47e5762b.png\" title=\"Chris21_0-1775856334974.png\"/></span></p><p>which could be misinterpreted.</p><p> </p></div>",
                    "author": "Chris21",
                    "role": "Associate II"
                }
            ],
